From 65b0bf657ef75274290c568fcd2931817712f42e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Phase14 audit <audit@local>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 06:27:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10/20] content(claims): remove the remaining factory / line /
 country figures from meta, video schema and LP diagrams
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Follow-up to the B3 capability-claims batch (audit Phase 4 C-01..C-05):
a build-wide sweep found the same undocumented figures on four more
surfaces that the JSON/component pass did not reach.
- homepage meta description (PAGE_DESCRIPTION_OVERRIDES['/']): 'Two
  Shenzhen factories, 10 automated production lines, 305+ pieces of
  equipment … 50+ countries' -> product families + certified systems (155 ch)
- homepage VideoObject.description: same figures removed; footage described
  as supplied by Proud Tek rather than asserting facility ownership
- 3 /lp/ hero diagrams (SVG text + <desc>): '10 lines, 2 sites', '2 factories
  · 10 lines', 'To 50+ countries', '2 Shenzhen sites · 10 automated lines' and
  the 'no subcontracted production' footer rewritten to the certified-scope /
  'specified, controlled and documented by Proud Tek' wording
- /lp/rfid-manufacturer-shenzhen/: the matching 'no subcontracted step'
  sentence softened the same way
The wider 'in-house / own-the-line' narrative (75 editorial files) is left
for the owner decision recorded in the Phase 14 report (D-04).
